# SFT execution status v0.117

2026-09-26. Finalized write-topology endpoints can now move into consuming
guardian, broker, worker and controller components through one-shot descriptor
authorities. **This fixes the socket-object/double-close gap discovered during
composition review, but it does not yet fork or run the process composition;
Gate 5 remains incomplete.** No real socket, descriptor, process, thread,
pidfd, signal, waitid, cgroup, listener, payload, remote mutation, GPU
operation, inference or training occurred.

## Completed

- Only an exact frozen topology in `controller`, `broker`, `worker` or
  `guardian_watch` final state can transfer an endpoint, and only an endpoint
  assigned to that role is eligible.
- The topology owner, lock, deadline and socket identity are revalidated before
  mutation. The endpoint is removed before its single detach attempt, so the
  topology cannot later close the transferred descriptor or retry ambiguity.
- A failed detach retains the socket object. A failed identity check after
  detach retains the raw descriptor and expected identity; it is not closed as
  a possible reused descriptor.
- A successful detach creates one private authority with no FD or identity in
  its snapshot. It can either transfer the descriptor once or close it once.
- Transfer checks identity before releasing prior ownership. Close revokes
  ownership and consumes the attempt before its final identity check, so a
  changed descriptor is never closed and an ambiguous close cannot be retried.
- Every endpoint assigned to all four final roles was exercised. The frozen
  topology and all v0.115/v0.116 evidence remain byte-for-byte unchanged.

## Verification

**896 unique tests pass on CPython 3.11.15 and 3.13.7**, with no failures,
errors or skips: 18 new authority-transfer tests plus the previous 878
regressions. All new runtime, socket, descriptor, process-identity, clock and
close boundaries are synthetic.

Syntax/AST checks pass for both new files on both runtimes; maximum line length
is 84 and trailing whitespace is zero. Tests used `-B`, and no bytecode file
for the new component is present. The six predecessor-plan bindings and all
five new-plan bindings match their recorded sizes and SHA-256 values.

