## Exact next work and unchanged boundary

The next successor can now implement the fully doubled private composition:
controller forks and pidfd-binds guardian; guardian adopts its prefork topology,
creates the lease, forks and pidfd-binds broker and worker; each process moves
to its exact final set and transfers only the endpoints its fixed component
will consume. One identity-checked duplicate is still required when another
component must borrow a child owner's pidfd.

After the fork composition, one fixed controller event loop must verify READY
before guardian arm, reserve aggregate bytes and receive ACK before each broker
CONTINUE, verify CONSUMED, collect terminal reports and enforce deadline
cleanup. Listener/drop/seal/full-size bootstrap integration and separately
authorized Linux native qualification still follow.

GPU is still unnecessary. No S3 or other remote availability check was made.
Real import, training and production remain disabled. The new source, test and
three records are local and untracked; nothing was staged, committed or pushed.
